! Radial cascade at 0.47 deg, level 3 TEST (2026-11-25): 168 cells (top at
! 0.998 R, -1.5 Mm), imported from casc047_l2test's export (t = 1 yr + 10 d),
! for 2 days. The pile-up question without any fix: does the near-top field
! under the conductor grow beyond B_eq (L2 test: rms B_h 1.4 kG, B/B_eq 0.37
! at its top; B_h ~flat at ~750 G in the bulk while rho drops)? At this top
! B_eq ~0.4-0.9 kG (v 0.7-1.5 km/s), v_A(1.4 kG) ~2.2 km/s.
! - Import as casc047_l2test: cells 1-140 (all variables) from the export,
!   141-168 from the init file at rest with B = 0; b_seed 'none' (else the seed
!   is added to the imported field). Conductor top, no b_top_beq.
! - 1.875 deg stand-in: dt 5.9 s at the start (radial wave at cell 168, dr 92
!   km, 7.7 km/s); expect ~4 s once the flows and v_A grow (L2: 29 -> 17 s).
!   ~5e-4 SU per step (L1's per cell x 168/112): ~11 SU and ~0.9 h per day on
!   6 nodes: 2 days ~22 SU, ~2 h.
! - RAN WITH va_max = 1.0e6 (10 km/s; removed from this file 2026-11-25): the
!   cap acted at the top and the run hit NaN at day 11.48. Reruns without it:
!   casc047_l3nocap, casc047_l3beq.
! - Needs casc047_l2test's state_export_r*.bin (written at its end).
!   sbatch -N 6 --ntasks-per-node 96 -t 03:30:00 tools/job.stampede3_seq runs/casc047_l3test.nml
&cz3d
  import_dir = '/scratch/09595/xianyu2023/CZTR_3D_out/casc047_l2test'
  grid_file = 'data/grid_atm20.dat', init_file = 'data/init_wind20_dip_m600.dat', n_r_cells = 168
  table_file = 'data/eos_table_wind.bin'
  out_dir = '/scratch/09595/xianyu2023/CZTR_3D_out/casc047_l3test'
  wall_top = 'face'
  top_energy = 'cooling', cool_width_hp = 1.0, grey_top_km = 1000.0
  use_convection = .false.
  rsst_depth_km = 500.0, rsst_q = -0.5, rsst_form = 'hotta2012'
  diffusion_heating = .true.
  ds1_random = 1.0
  yy_margin = 0, n_theta = 48, n_phi = 144, nb_theta = 8, nb_phi = 24, refine_h = 2, nb_r = 28
  use_atmosphere = .false.
  use_B = .true., b_seed = 'none', b_bc_bottom = 'conductor', b_bc_top = 'conductor'
  si_radial = .true., b_diff_form = 'resistive', b_eta_dr = 1.0
  omega_rot = 2.6e-6, lz_correct_steps = 20
  dt1 = 0.0, mr_levels = 0
  t_end = 3.25968e7, n_step_max = 100000000, dt_max = 1.0e4
  n_log = 100, dt_prof = 0.0, prof_every = 300, plot_dt = 0.0, restart_dt = 86400.0
  dump_shells = 112, 140, 141, 154, 162, 168
  wall_time_margin = 1800.0
  export_state = .true.
/
